    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWith `relativenumber` option on, it looks like this:\n\n```\n2 <- I want to move to this line\n1\n0 <- current line\n1\n2\n```\n\nThe problem is that, when I switched from another terminal tab, I often miss my current position and use wrong command. In this case, I should use `2k` but I sometimes use `2j` instead.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhat about this?\n\n```\n+2\n+1\n0\n-1\n-2\n```\n\nWith this, even when I miss my current position, it's easier to tell if I should use `2k` or `2j`.\nThe drawback is the increase of column width. I believe it's not such a big problem with modern large screens, but this should not be the default when we set `relativenumber` option.\n\n### Proposal on option\n\nCurrently, `relativenumber` option is a boolean option. I'd like to propose a third valid value, `signed`. When `signed` is set to `relativenumber` option, it adds the direction sign (`+` and `-`) to the relative line number.",
